  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;be the mirror image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;with respect to the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. If a line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;meets the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
