  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/39a46925-3249-4858-98b3-603eef5c8cc3-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 162px;\" /></p><p>Let parallel vector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>As&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is the mirror image on given plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Let the vector parallel to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Let point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;lying on plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, so, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />So, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>",
